                <pb facs="0631" n="513" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg513"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/859: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Perkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-09-23T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 23,
                                1928—noon</hi>.</date><lb/>[Received September 24—9:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>724. Department’s 323, September 20, 5 [<hi rendition="#italic">8</hi>] p.m. In
                    conversation with Admiral Bristol I have acquainted him with the Department’s
                    views regarding the use of naval forces in preventing taxation <pb facs="0632"
                        n="514" xml:id="pg514"/> and regarding private taxation arrangements as set
                    forth in paragraph 7 of the Department’s telegram above mentioned. I have also
                    made available to him the text of the Department’s two telegrams to the Legation
                    referred to in that paragraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
